    "body": "### What happens?\n\nExecuting a query that includes a correlated scalar subquery using the spatial extension (ST_Intersects / ST_Point / ST_GeomFromText) combined with LEFT JOIN and GROUP BY ALL causes DuckDB to crash (segmentation fault) when the joined table produces NULL values.\n\nExpected Behavior\nThe query should complete successfully and return:\n\nActual Behavior\nDuckDB crashes immediately (Segmentation Fault / Process termination) upon query execution.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```\nLOAD spatial;\n\n-- 1. Create and populate 'fire'\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE fire (\n    ShooterId TEXT,\n    MunitionId TEXT\n);\nINSERT INTO fire VALUES ('2074', '2062');\n\n-- 2. Create empty 'Detonation' table (causes NULLs on LEFT JOIN)\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE Detonation (\n    ShooterId TEXT,\n    MunitionId TEXT,\n    Longitude DOUBLE,\n    Latitude DOUBLE\n);\n\n-- 3. Create and populate 'oparea'\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE oparea (\n    name TEXT,\n    area TEXT\n);\nINSERT INTO oparea (name, area)\nVALUES ('xxxx', 'POLYGON((80 40,90 40,85 35,85 40,80 40))');\n\n-- 4. Query triggering the crash\nSELECT\n    Detonation.Longitude,\n    Detonation.Latitude,\n    IFNULL((\n        SELECT FIRST(name)\n        FROM oparea\n        WHERE ST_Intersects(\n            ST_GeomFromText(area), \n            ST_Point(Detonation.Longitude, Detonation.Latitude)\n        )\n    ), 'Other') AS area_name\nFROM fire\nLEFT JOIN Detonation\n    ON fire.ShooterId = Detonation.ShooterId\n    AND fire.MunitionId = Detonation.MunitionId\nGROUP BY ALL;\n```\n\n### OS:\n\nGeneric\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nGeneric\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nRobotSlacker\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nN/A\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nYes",
